@page "/engagement"

<PageTitle>Work With The Singularity Workshop | Engagements</PageTitle>

<div class="engagement-page">
    <section class="engagement-hero">
        <p class="eyebrow">THE WORKSHOP IS OPEN</p>
        <h1>Let's build the thing<br /><span>that fixes the problem.</span></h1>
        <p class="lead-copy">
            You don't need a perfect specification. You don't even need to know what the solution should be.
            Bring the workflow, the bottleneck, the system that keeps fighting you, or the idea that nobody else knows how to build.
        </p>
        <div class="hero-actions">
            <a class="action primary" href="mailto:thesingularityworkshop@gmail.com?subject=Schedule%20a%20Workshop%20Engagement&amp;body=I'd%20like%20to%20schedule%20a%20Workshop%20engagement.%0A%0AThe%20problem%20I'd%20like%20to%20discuss%3A%0A">Request a Time <span>→</span></a>
            <a class="action secondary" href="/#proof">See the Evidence <span>↓</span></a>
        </div>
    </section>

    <section class="diagnostic-section">
        <div class="section-heading">
            <p class="eyebrow">THE FIRST STEP</p>
            <h2>A focused diagnostic.</h2>
            <p>
                We start by understanding what is actually happening. What are people doing? What systems are involved?
                Where does information get lost? Where does a human have to intervene? What does the current solution cost?
            </p>
        </div>

        <div class="diagnostic-grid">
            <div class="diagnostic-card">
                <span>01</span>
                <h3>Show me the workflow.</h3>
                <p>Screen share it. Draw it. Send the ugly spreadsheet. Walk me through the process that everyone has learned to hate.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="diagnostic-card">
                <span>02</span>
                <h3>Find the leverage.</h3>
                <p>We'll identify the repetitive work, fragile boundaries, missing data, architectural bottlenecks, and opportunities for automation.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="diagnostic-card">
                <span>03</span>
                <h3>Decide whether to build.</h3>
                <p>If the numbers don't make sense, I'll tell you. If they do, we can define a focused engagement and build the smallest useful thing first.</p>
            </div>
        </div>
    </section>

    <section class="engagement-types">
        <div class="section-heading centered">
            <p class="eyebrow">WHAT WE CAN DO TOGETHER</p>
            <h2>From one ugly problem<br /><span>to an entire system.</span></h2>
        </div>

        <div class="type-grid">
            <article>
                <div class="type-code">DIAGNOSTIC</div>
                <h3>Architecture &amp; Automation Review</h3>
                <p>Understand the problem, map the workflow, inspect the technical boundary, and leave with a credible implementation path.</p>
            </article>
            <article>
                <div class="type-code">BUILD</div>
                <h3>Focused Engineering Engagement</h3>
                <p>Build a bounded piece of software: an integration, automation, tool, API, state system, data pipeline, performance fix, or prototype.</p>
            </article>
            <article>
                <div class="type-code">R&amp;D</div>
                <h3>Systems Architecture</h3>
                <p>When the problem is larger than a feature, we'll design the machinery: boundaries, data, execution, state, lifecycle, and the path from prototype to product.</p>
            </article>
        </div>
    </section>

    <section class="why-section">
        <div class="why-panel">
            <div>
                <p class="eyebrow">WHY THE WORKSHOP</p>
                <h2>Software engineering with a field engineer's instinct.</h2>
            </div>
            <div class="why-copy">
                <p>
                    I've spent more than 15 years working inside complicated AEC/BIM environments, where software has to survive real projects,
                    real people, real data, and real deadlines. That domain experience became the laboratory for a much broader software-engineering practice.
                </p>
                <p>
                    Today the Workshop works across .NET, architecture, automation, AI/agent systems, performance engineering, simulation,
                    Unity, WebAssembly, and whatever boundary the problem happens to cross.
                </p>
                <p class="accent-copy">The technology is the tool. The problem is the target.</p>
            </div>
        </div>
    </section>

    <section class="close-section">
        <p class="eyebrow">READY WHEN YOU ARE</p>
        <h2>Tell me what hurts.</h2>
        <p>
            Send a short description of the problem and a good way to reach you. We'll take it from there.
        </p>
        <a class="action primary large" href="mailto:thesingularityworkshop@gmail.com?subject=The%20Singularity%20Workshop%20-%20New%20Engagement&amp;body=Name%3A%0ACompany%3A%0A%0AWhat%20problem%20are%20you%20trying%20to%20solve%3F%0A%0AWhat%20does%20the%20current%20workflow%20look%20like%3F%0A%0AHow%20can%20we%20reach%20you%3F%0A">Start the Conversation <span>→</span></a>
    </section>
</div>

<style>
    .engagement-page {
        --ink: #08070d;
        --panel: #11101a;
        --cyan: #00ffcc;
        --magenta: #ff2bd6;
        --violet: #9b5cff;
        --muted: #aaa7b6;
        margin: -1.5rem -1.5rem 0;
        min-height: 100vh;
        color: #fff;
        background: var(--ink);
        font-family: Inter, ui-sans-serif, system-ui, -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, "Segoe UI", sans-serif;
    }

    .engagement-hero {
        padding: 7rem 9vw 6rem;
        background: radial-gradient(circle at 80% 20%, rgba(155,92,255,.18), transparent 28%), radial-gradient(circle at 15% 70%, rgba(0,255,204,.08), transparent 30%), #08070d;
        border-bottom: 1px solid rgba(0,255,204,.18);
    }

    .eyebrow { color: #8f8ca2; font-size: .7rem; font-weight: 900; letter-spacing: .18em; }
    .engagement-hero h1 { max-width: 1000px; font-size: clamp(3.3rem, 7vw, 6.7rem); line-height: .92; letter-spacing: -.055em; margin: 1rem 0 2rem; font-weight: 900; }
    .engagement-hero h1 span, .section-heading h2 span { color: var(--cyan); }
    .lead-copy { max-width: 820px; color: #c2bfcb; font-size: 1.2rem; line-height: 1.8; }

    .hero-actions { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 1rem; margin-top: 2rem; }
    .action { display: inline-flex; align-items: center; justify-content: space-between; gap: 1.5rem; padding: 1rem 1.5rem; border-radius: 5px; text-decoration: none; font-weight: 900; transition: .2s; }
    .action.primary { color: #04110d; background: var(--cyan); box-shadow: 0 0 35px rgba(0,255,204,.2); }
    .action.primary:hover { color: #04110d; transform: translateY(-3px); box-shadow: 0 12px 40px rgba(0,255,204,.3); }
    .action.secondary { color: #fff; border: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,.2); background: rgba(255,255,255,.03); }
    .action.secondary:hover { color: #fff; transform: translateY(-3px); border-color: var(--cyan); }
    .action.large { padding: 1.2rem 1.7rem; }

    .diagnostic-section, .engagement-types, .why-section { padding: 7rem 9vw; }
    .diagnostic-section { background: #10101a; }
    .section-heading { max-width: 800px; margin-bottom: 3rem; }
    .section-heading.centered { text-align: center; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto; }
    .section-heading h2 { font-size: clamp(2.6rem, 5vw, 4.5rem); line-height: .98; letter-spacing: -.045em; margin: .6rem 0 1.4rem; }
    .section-heading p:last-child { color: var(--muted); line-height: 1.8; font-size: 1.05rem; }

    .diagnostic-grid, .type-grid { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr); gap: 1rem; max-width: 1200px; margin: auto; }
    .diagnostic-card, .type-grid article { padding: 2.2rem; min-height: 280px; border: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,.09); border-radius: 8px; background: rgba(255,255,255,.025); }
    .diagnostic-card span, .type-code { color: var(--magenta); font-family: ui-monospace, monospace; font-size: .7rem; letter-spacing: .14em; font-weight: 900; }
    .diagnostic-card h3, .type-grid h3 { font-size: 1.45rem; margin: 2.3rem 0 1rem; }
    .diagnostic-card p, .type-grid p { color: var(--muted); line-height: 1.75; }

    .engagement-types { background: #08070d; }
    .type-grid article { min-height: 250px; background: linear-gradient(145deg, rgba(155,92,255,.06), rgba(255,255,255,.015)); }
    .type-grid h3 { margin-top: 1.4rem; }

    .why-section { background: linear-gradient(180deg, #11101a, #08070d); }
    .why-panel { max-width: 1200px; margin: auto; display: grid; grid-template-columns: .9fr 1.1fr; gap: 5rem; align-items: start; }
    .why-panel h2 { font-size: clamp(2.3rem, 4vw, 4rem); line-height: 1; letter-spacing: -.04em; margin-top: .7rem; }
    .why-copy { color: var(--muted); line-height: 1.8; font-size: 1.02rem; }
    .accent-copy { color: var(--cyan); font-size: 1.25rem; font-weight: 800; border-left: 2px solid var(--magenta); padding-left: 1rem; }

    .close-section { padding: 8rem 9vw; text-align: center; background: radial-gradient(circle at 50% 20%, rgba(255,43,214,.16), transparent 40%), #07060b; border-top: 1px solid rgba(255,43,214,.18); }
    .close-section h2 { font-size: clamp(3.2rem, 7vw, 6.5rem); line-height: .9; letter-spacing: -.055em; margin: .8rem 0 1.5rem; }
    .close-section > p:not(.eyebrow) { max-width: 650px; margin: 0 auto 2rem; color: var(--muted); line-height: 1.8; }

    @@media (max-width: 850px) {
        .diagnostic-grid, .type-grid, .why-panel { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
        .why-panel { gap: 2rem; }
    }

    @@media (max-width: 600px) {
        .engagement-hero, .diagnostic-section, .engagement-types, .why-section, .close-section { padding-left: 7vw; padding-right: 7vw; }
        .hero-actions { flex-direction: column; }
        .action { width: 100%; }
    }
</style>
